  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Monday) \nIssued at 1259 AM MDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nShower and thunderstorm coverage and rainfall intensity will trend\ndownward Friday afternoon and evening as the amplitude of the\nupper high decreases and an east-to-west ridge axis develops \nallowing drier air to move over western and northern parts of the \nstate. Storm coverage will then increase over central and western\nareas Saturday, and especially Sunday, as the upper high drifts\neastward toward the lower Mississippi River valley, enabling a\nmore traditional plume of monsoon moisture to set up. Models vary\non how well the monsoon plume will remain over the forecast area\non Monday, depending on how deeply an upper level trough digs over\nthe west coast. \n\nOtherwise, record and near-record high temperatures are forecast\nto continue through the end of this week. Temperatures will trend\ncloser to average early next week over western areas with the \narrival of the monsoon moisture plume, while eastern readings \nclimb around 10 degrees above average.",
